cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the paper below."
type: software
title: "Code accompanying: Conformational Dynamics and Disorder of HPV-16 E6"
version: 1.0.0
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and simulation input files for the J. Phys. Chem. B paper
  "Conformational Dynamics and Disorder of HPV-16 E6". Includes Desmond inputs
  for 35 µs of unbiased MD and five well-tempered metadynamics replicates of
  apo HPV-16 E6, and scripts for Markov state modeling, metadynamics free-energy
  surfaces, secondary structure, structural observables, BioEmu ensemble
  metrics, and SPARTA+/Delta2D comparison with NMR chemical shifts.
  MD trajectories are archived separately on Zenodo.
keywords:
  - HPV-16 E6
  - molecular dynamics
  - intrinsically disordered regions
  - metadynamics
  - Markov state model
  - BioEmu
